{
  "$schema": "./node_modules/oxlint/configuration_schema.json",
  "plugins": ["typescript", "unicorn", "oxc"],
  "categories": {
    "correctness": "error",
    "suspicious": "warn"
  },
  "ignorePatterns": [
    "**/node_modules/**",
    "**/dist/**",
    "**/build/**",
    "**/.next/**",
    "**/.wxt/**",
    "**/.output/**",
    "packages/contracts/src/**"
  ],
  "rules": {
    "no-console": "off",
    "typescript/no-explicit-any": "warn"
  },
  "overrides": [
    {
      "comment": "A Nest module is a class with nothing in it by design — the decorator is the whole declaration. Scoped to module files so an accidentally empty class anywhere else is still caught.",
      "files": ["**/*.module.ts"],
      "rules": {
        "typescript/no-extraneous-class": "off"
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "Constitution IX, the driver half. Expressed entirely as `patterns` and with no `paths` key, and that is load-bearing: oxlint ignores `patterns` outright when `paths` is also present, so the `mongoose/*` and `@prisma/client/*` half of this rule had been inert since P0 - only the bare specifiers were ever checked. A deep import was refused by nothing. `patterns` matches a bare specifier as well, so one key does both. Probed after every change to it.",
      "files": [
        "backend/src/contexts/**/domain/**",
        "backend/src/contexts/**/features/**",
        "backend/src/shared/cqrs/**",
        "backend/src/shared/auth/**",
        "backend/src/shared/time/**"
      ],
      "rules": {
        "no-restricted-imports": [
          "error",
          {
            "patterns": [
              {
                "group": [
                  "mongoose",
                  "mongoose/**",
                  "mongodb",
                  "mongodb/**",
                  "@prisma/client",
                  "@prisma/client/**"
                ],
                "message": "Constitution IX: a database driver belongs in infrastructure/. Declare a repository or unit-of-work port in domain/ and bind an adapter in the context module, one per store."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "comment": "A context's domain/ and features/ may not reach into another context, and still may not import a driver. Both are repeated here rather than left to the override above, because two overrides setting the same rule may replace rather than merge, and a config change that silently switched the driver rule off would be worse than the gap it closed. This is the rule that was missing when Identity imported Operations' AuditPort while OperationsModule imported IdentityModule back: the graph stopped resolving in both roles and nothing but a boot failure said why. infrastructure/ is deliberately absent from the file list - an adapter binding a local port to another context is the sanctioned seam, and admin-device.lookup.ts and admin-password.probe.ts are exactly that. The context names are enumerated rather than matched with a wildcard, and that is not laziness in the config - the depth that means \"a sibling context\" differs by where the file sits (`../../Y` from domain/, `../../../Y` from features/<slice>/), so a blanket `../../*` would also forbid a slice importing its own context's domain/. Enumerating costs a dozen patterns per context and is provably right; the wildcard is shorter and wrong. What enumerating does not do is maintain itself - `meetings` landed in P5 without its twelve lines and nothing failed, because a missing name makes the rule silent rather than red, and the unpoliced direction was the reverse one: nothing stopped another context importing `../../meetings/**`. So this group is now GENERATED from the directory listing of backend/src/contexts/ by `infra/gen-lint-contexts.mjs`; do not hand-edit it. `pnpm lint:contexts` is the CI step that fails when it falls behind the tree, `pnpm lint:contexts:write` regenerates it, and the rule is still probed by writing a file that should fail and checking it does.",
      "files": [
        "backend/src/contexts/*/domain/**",
        "backend/src/contexts/*/features/**"
      ],
      "rules": {
        "no-restricted-imports": [
          "error",
          {
            "patterns": [
              {
                "group": [
                  "mongoose",
                  "mongoose/**",
                  "mongodb",
                  "mongodb/**",
                  "@prisma/client",
                  "@prisma/client/**"
                ],
                "message": "Constitution IX: a database driver belongs in infrastructure/. Declare a repository or unit-of-work port in domain/ and bind an adapter in the context module, one per store."
              },
              {
                "group": [
                  "../../conversations",
                  "../../conversations/**",
                  "../../../conversations",
                  "../../../conversations/**",
                  "../../../../conversations",
                  "../../../../conversations/**",
                  "../../../contexts/conversations",
                  "../../../contexts/conversations/**",
                  "../../../../contexts/conversations",
                  "../../../../contexts/conversations/**",
                  "../../../../../contexts/conversations",
                  "../../../../../contexts/conversations/**",
                  "../../identity",
                  "../../identity/**",
                  "../../../identity",
                  "../../../identity/**",
                  "../../../../identity",
                  "../../../../identity/**",
                  "../../../contexts/identity",
                  "../../../contexts/identity/**",
                  "../../../../contexts/identity",
                  "../../../../contexts/identity/**",
                  "../../../../../contexts/identity",
                  "../../../../../contexts/identity/**",
                  "../../knowledge",
                  "../../knowledge/**",
                  "../../../knowledge",
                  "../../../knowledge/**",
                  "../../../../knowledge",
                  "../../../../knowledge/**",
                  "../../../contexts/knowledge",
                  "../../../contexts/knowledge/**",
                  "../../../../contexts/knowledge",
                  "../../../../contexts/knowledge/**",
                  "../../../../../contexts/knowledge",
                  "../../../../../contexts/knowledge/**",
                  "../../meetings",
                  "../../meetings/**",
                  "../../../meetings",
                  "../../../meetings/**",
                  "../../../../meetings",
                  "../../../../meetings/**",
                  "../../../contexts/meetings",
                  "../../../contexts/meetings/**",
                  "../../../../contexts/meetings",
                  "../../../../contexts/meetings/**",
                  "../../../../../contexts/meetings",
                  "../../../../../contexts/meetings/**",
                  "../../notifications",
                  "../../notifications/**",
                  "../../../notifications",
                  "../../../notifications/**",
                  "../../../../notifications",
                  "../../../../notifications/**",
                  "../../../contexts/notifications",
                  "../../../contexts/notifications/**",
                  "../../../../contexts/notifications",
                  "../../../../contexts/notifications/**",
                  "../../../../../contexts/notifications",
                  "../../../../../contexts/notifications/**",
                  "../../nutrition",
                  "../../nutrition/**",
                  "../../../nutrition",
                  "../../../nutrition/**",
                  "../../../../nutrition",
                  "../../../../nutrition/**",
                  "../../../contexts/nutrition",
                  "../../../contexts/nutrition/**",
                  "../../../../contexts/nutrition",
                  "../../../../contexts/nutrition/**",
                  "../../../../../contexts/nutrition",
                  "../../../../../contexts/nutrition/**",
                  "../../operations",
                  "../../operations/**",
                  "../../../operations",
                  "../../../operations/**",
                  "../../../../operations",
                  "../../../../operations/**",
                  "../../../contexts/operations",
                  "../../../contexts/operations/**",
                  "../../../../contexts/operations",
                  "../../../../contexts/operations/**",
                  "../../../../../contexts/operations",
                  "../../../../../contexts/operations/**",
                  "../../planning",
                  "../../planning/**",
                  "../../../planning",
                  "../../../planning/**",
                  "../../../../planning",
                  "../../../../planning/**",
                  "../../../contexts/planning",
                  "../../../contexts/planning/**",
                  "../../../../contexts/planning",
                  "../../../../contexts/planning/**",
                  "../../../../../contexts/planning",
                  "../../../../../contexts/planning/**",
                  "../../profile",
                  "../../profile/**",
                  "../../../profile",
                  "../../../profile/**",
                  "../../../../profile",
                  "../../../../profile/**",
                  "../../../contexts/profile",
                  "../../../contexts/profile/**",
                  "../../../../contexts/profile",
                  "../../../../contexts/profile/**",
                  "../../../../../contexts/profile",
                  "../../../../../contexts/profile/**",
                  "../../reminders",
                  "../../reminders/**",
                  "../../../reminders",
                  "../../../reminders/**",
                  "../../../../reminders",
                  "../../../../reminders/**",
                  "../../../contexts/reminders",
                  "../../../contexts/reminders/**",
                  "../../../../contexts/reminders",
                  "../../../../contexts/reminders/**",
                  "../../../../../contexts/reminders",
                  "../../../../../contexts/reminders/**",
                  "../../rhythm",
                  "../../rhythm/**",
                  "../../../rhythm",
                  "../../../rhythm/**",
                  "../../../../rhythm",
                  "../../../../rhythm/**",
                  "../../../contexts/rhythm",
                  "../../../contexts/rhythm/**",
                  "../../../../contexts/rhythm",
                  "../../../../contexts/rhythm/**",
                  "../../../../../contexts/rhythm",
                  "../../../../../contexts/rhythm/**",
                  "../../sync",
                  "../../sync/**",
                  "../../../sync",
                  "../../../sync/**",
                  "../../../../sync",
                  "../../../../sync/**",
                  "../../../contexts/sync",
                  "../../../contexts/sync/**",
                  "../../../../contexts/sync",
                  "../../../../contexts/sync/**",
                  "../../../../../contexts/sync",
                  "../../../../../contexts/sync/**",
                  "../../training",
                  "../../training/**",
                  "../../../training",
                  "../../../training/**",
                  "../../../../training",
                  "../../../../training/**",
                  "../../../contexts/training",
                  "../../../contexts/training/**",
                  "../../../../contexts/training",
                  "../../../../contexts/training/**",
                  "../../../../../contexts/training",
                  "../../../../../contexts/training/**"
                ],
                "message": "Constitution IX: a context may not import another context. Cross-context needs go through a QueryBus call, an outbox event, or a port declared here and bound to an adapter in this context's own infrastructure/ - the one layer allowed to know another context exists. A helper three contexts want belongs in shared/."
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
